{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01ANwRm2VQhcsSD1DseqQjrP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## rnd-v1 â€” Build Trio Session Summary\n\n**Goal:** Build the v1 Anchor R&D Control Surface (durable trio-job control plane) wave-by-wave under the Foreman EXECUTE â†’ ADVERSARIAL-REVIEW â†’ FIX â†’ JUDGE loop. All waves below reached GO.\n\n**Grounded claims:**\n\n- **Wave 2 â€” Foundations (GO after 1 fix iter):** Added `paths.py` (lazy `ANCHOR_DATA_DIR`, `ensure_data_dirs()`, re-entrant `WRITE_LOCK`, `auth_ok()`/`expected_token()`, `bind_with_retry()`, idempotent `migrate_data()`); moved `anchor_gui.py` to `ThreadingHTTPServer` with `@_with_write_lock` on all mutators and a token gate atop `do_POST`. MINOR-1 (import-time mkdir) closed â†’ now lazy. Gate GREEN, 22 passed.\n\n- **Wave 3 â€” Registry + New-Project flow + per-project store (GO after 1 fix iter):** Added `rnd_registry.py` (id-keyed, non-unique `folder_path`, CRUD + `group_by_folder`, retain-not-delete lifecycle, per-project `.anchor/projects/<id>/{research,planning,build,deliverables,jobs}/` scaffold, idempotent legacy-id assignment, all writes under `WRITE_LOCK`) and `dir_browser.py`. `anchor_gui.py` gained the New-Project flow, `/project/<id>` route, and folder-grouped tiles with a 4-state status line.\n\n- **Wave 4 â€” Mock runner + launch/tail primitive, the durable-job keystone (GO, 0 fix iters):** Added `job_runner.py` â€” `ANCHOR_RUNNER_CMD`-indirected launch, durable per-job log + ring buffer (deque maxlen 5000), `long_poll(?since=K)`, `cancel()` via `taskkill /T /F` (sets `cancelled` before kill; `_finalize` won't clobber terminal status), `liveness_check`/`reconcile_on_startup` â†’ `interrupted`. Job store under `ANCHOR_DATA_DIR/rnd_jobs/` with atomic tmpâ†’replace. Added deterministic `tests/fake_claude.py`.\n\n- **Wave 5 â€” Gate adapter / in-session answers (GO after 1 fix iter):** The captured `crucible_gate.jsonl` fixture was absent, so the wave authored a faithful deterministic 6-line stream-json fixture modeling the documented `AskUserQuestion` frame (no live claude). Added `gate_adapter.py` â€” parses stream-json into a prompt-box record `{question, options, tool_use_id, header, multiSelect}`; `mark_awaiting_input` persists `state=awaiting-input`.\n\n- **Wave 6 â€” Lane wiring + concurrency (GO, 0 fix iters):** Added `lanes.py` with the frozen lane map (researchâ†’researchPrime / planâ†’crucible / buildâ†’foreman) and `launch_lane()` (resolves project, scaffolds, passes per-project output dir via `--skill/--output-dir/--prompt-seed`, writes `launch.pointer.json` as on-disk proof; research no-gate, plan/build gate-in-session). `job_runner.py` concurrency: `_ACTIVE_LANE` keyed `(project_id,lane)` (same-lane serialize, cross-lane concurrent) and `_FOLDER_BUILD` keyed `folder_path`.\n\n- **Wave 7 â€” Versioned history + report viewer + cost rollup + auto-commit (GO after 1 fix iter):** Added `effort_history.py` (job-id-scoped append-only pointer-records, index reversed on read so index 0 is newest, nothing deleted on re-run, cost capture from the result envelope, per-effortâ†’laneâ†’project rollups, scoped per-effort git auto-commit with no push). Added `report_viewer.py` (PDF-by-default, else stdlib mdâ†’HTML reader with KaTeX, traversal-safe) and vendored real KaTeX 0.16.11.\n\n- **Wave 8 â€” Shareable, data-free distribution (GO after 1 fix iter):** Added `distro.py` (deny-by-default manifest staging + no-personal-data scan), `dist_manifest.txt`, and planted-secret fixtures. **Both reviewers initially NO-GO:** BLOCKER-1 â€” `distro.py` hard-coded the literal `john.liechty@gmail.com` and shipped it (C10 PII leak, passing only via self-suppression); MAJOR-1 â€” the `distro-scan: allow` marker was globally exploitable (any staged file self-grants a leak, reproduced end-to-end); MAJOR-2 â€” the token scan missed unquoted secrets. Fixed to GO.\n\n- **Wave 9 â€” Deliverables + taskâ†”project activation, TERMINAL (GO, 0 fix iters):** Added `deliverables.py` with per-type success contracts (doc=exists+nonempty; script/skill=exit 0 AND `is_error`-clear; program=exit 0 within timeout), enforcing stdin=DEVNULL, non-interactive, timeout, and tree-kill reap (no orphan). `anchor_gui.py` gained the project-tasks view (filtered by parsed `Project:` field), deliverables render, and token-gated `link_task`/`run_deliverable`; `anchor.py` gained the `link_task`/`link` CLI.\n\n**Errors/risks surfaced:** The Wave-8 PII-leak and exploitable-allow-marker blockers were the most serious findings; both were caught by independent refute-mode review and resolved before the wave passed. Wave 5 required authoring a missing test fixture rather than using a captured one."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4253,"cache_creation_input_tokens":51493,"cache_read_input_tokens":20861,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":51493},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7ec42652-9b54-4ad8-b053-2f1652128f56","uuid":"0e08712d-e7ba-4735-8060-24502e3374d9","request_id":"req_011Cc9RsRyrGzMmrxfa9YgZK"}
